 "notes": "Class-by-class mapping comes from the comments in village.c and village_blocks.c. test_structures checks the piece trees against out/java/structures/vi-*; test_villagers (out/java/villagers) exercises the villagers the houses spawn; I did not read those manifests in full or run any test. The Java piece classes Road and Path share native V_ROAD. GPU note: pieces are heap-allocated and the pending queues are realloc'd pointer lists (village.c village_pending_add). Closed by lane/idxworld (verification): the piece trees against out/java/structures (vi-2, vi-42), the blocks against the populate dumps, the villagers against out/java/villagers, and a village saved mid-population and resumed by struct-cp-s42 and persist-village-s42. lane/villagetrade 2026-09-27: the tail-only evidence (X-01/X-02) now points at the full re-records persist-village-full-s42, whose native replay starts before the behaviour."
